/target
Cargo.lock
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Gas Town per-worktree agent context — generated locally, never commit.
# Auto-checkpoint hooks run `git add -A`-style commits; without this entry
# the file leaks into WIP commits and collides with the untracked copy in
# every other polecat worktree on checkout.
CLAUDE.local.md

# wasm-bindgen output for the web playground (generated by the build)
/web/playground/pkg/

# web playground dependencies and build output
/web/playground/node_modules/
/web/playground/dist/

# wasm-bindgen output for the MCP server (generated by `npm run build`).
# Ignored from here rather than by the pkg/.gitignore wasm-pack writes: that
# nested file says `*`, and npm consults a package's own .gitignore when there
# is no .npmignore. Measured on npm 11.6.4: with `files: ["pkg/"]` that combination
# emits a tarball containing *zero* pkg files — no kernel, installs clean, throws
# MODULE_NOT_FOUND on first use. Listing the two wasm files individually (which
# package.json now does) survives it, but the trap is one refactor away, so
# build-wasm.mjs deletes the nested file and this entry does the ignoring instead
# (of-2y4.3).
/tools/mcp-server/pkg/
/tools/mcp-server/node_modules/

# Gas Town (added by gt)
.runtime/
.claude/
.logs/
__pycache__/
state.json
CLAUDE.md

# Mesh/BREP exports are build output, never source.
#
# The gallery's exports used to be committed under examples/output/ (103 MB, of
# which 91 MB was STEP). They are regenerated byte-for-byte differently whenever
# the STEP writer changes entity ordering, so every kernel change churned tens of
# megabytes and the checked-in copies drifted stale anyway. `npm run gallery`
# regenerates all of them in ~4 min (of-2y4.3).
#
# The PNG renders and manifest.json stay committed: they are small (376 KB
# total) and the transcripts embed the renders inline.
/*.stl
/*.step
/*.obj
/tools/mcp-server/examples/output/*.stl
/tools/mcp-server/examples/output/*.step
/tools/mcp-server/examples/output/*.obj
